  [38;5;246m1.[39m Env-driven, staging only (Recommended)
     [38;5;246mAdd a REPORTS_VERIFY_TLS env flag read in client.py, defaulting to True. sync_staging.py sets it False; [39m
     [38;5;246mexport_prod.py keeps full verification. Staging works, production stays protected.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Trust the staging cert
     [38;5;246mPoint verify at the staging CA/cert file via an env var (e.g. REPORTS_CA_BUNDLE) instead of turning verification [39m
     [38;5;246moff. Staging connections stay authenticated; needs the cert file available.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Blanket verify=False
     [38;5;246mExactly as asked: verify=False on both calls in client.py. Production report fetches also stop validating [39m
     [38;5;246mcertificates.[39m
